Quartic pentagon lower bounds for lambda two, three and four
==========================================================

Fixed source and current boundary
--------------------------------

F012 Table2, physical18, has three still-pending lower30 clauses for
(k,g,lambda)=(4,5,2),(4,5,3),(4,5,4). This route concerns only those existing
clauses. It reuses the vertex-ball argument and exact matching-forest
normalization from the completed lambda5 author packet. That packet awaits
distinct review and is not an accepted premise at this stage. The argument
below is written independently of its finite target; no target is started.

The single relevant order
-------------------------

Fix a root of a quartic graph with girth five and lambda pentagons through
each edge. Its Moore ball has the root, four parents and twelve leaves.
The six cross-branch matchings have sizes k_ij, with each row sum lambda.
As before, opposite sizes agree and their three distinct values a,b,c sum
to lambda, with each in 0..3. All branch permutations preserve the problem.
The total number of cross edges is 2lambda. Of the 36 leaf slots after the
parent edges, precisely 36-4lambda go to the exterior.

For t exterior vertices and e exterior edges, degree counting gives
4t=36-4lambda+2e. Hence e=2t-18+2lambda and n=17+t>=26-lambda.
The total number of pentagons is 2n lambda/5. For lambda2,3,4 this forces
5|n. Consequently the only order below30 consistent with these elementary
bounds is n25. At that order t8, e=2lambda-2, respectively2,4,6.

Therefore a complete exclusion at25 proves all three fixed lower30 claims.
The exterior inventory consists of every eight-vertex simple graph with
the indicated edge count, maximum degree at most four and girth at least
five. There are respectively C(28,2), C(28,4), C(28,6) labelled edge sets.
The last is376740, so this inventory is bounded before isomorphism reuse.
Do not presume all those exterior graphs are forests: cycles of length
five or six can occur in the six-edge case.

The complete boundary constructor remains the one proved for lambda5,
with the pentagon budget changed to the actual parameter. Every exterior
y takes 4-deg_H(y) old leaves, at most one per branch; all actual exterior
automorphisms act by relabelling. The monotonic cycle count and prefix
lexicographic tests are parameter-independent. Exact corresponding code
changes and meaningful controls must be checked before a bounded target.

No numerical lower bound or full-source credit is asserted by this note.
